    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Jake White names Ikanivere-led Fiji XV with Volavola and Lomani at half-back",
          "body": "Fiji head coach Jake White has made hooker Tevita Ikanivere captain for Saturday's Nations Championship test against Italy in Udine. Frank Lomani is at scrum-half and Ben Volavola, listed without a club, is at fly-half. Nathan Hughes starts at No. 8 and Josua Tuisova at inside centre, with Caleb Muntz among the replacements. Fiji are bottom of their pool without a point after last week's 15-43 defeat by Ireland in Dublin. They face a sixth-place play-off against Italy at Twickenham if they lose or win without a bonus point."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan moves to No. 8 against South Africa",
          "body": "Wales lose Adam Beard to shoulder injury before Australia test. New Zealand's Damian McKenzie replaces Richie Mo'unga at fly-half."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Bluenergy Stadium, Udine"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Referee row",
          "heading": "Steve Borthwick backs referees but declines to condemn Rassie Erasmus's claims",
          "body": "England head coach Steve Borthwick would not address claims by Springbok head coach Rassie Erasmus, banned for six matches by World Rugby, that referee Andrea Piardi and his assistants had shown France leniency. Instead, he urged respect for referees: \"I have absolute 100% confidence and faith that every match official in every game tries to do the very best they can.\" Naming his side for Saturday's All Blacks test, Borthwick also backed RFU referee Christophe Ridley, a regular at England's camp, for South Africa v Ireland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan moves to No. 8 against South Africa",
          "body": "Wales lose Adam Beard to shoulder injury before Australia test. New Zealand's Damian McKenzie replaces Richie Mo'unga at fly-half. Fiji make hooker Tevita Ikanivere captain for Italy test."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Twickenham, London"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tackle row",
          "heading": "Rugbyrama review backs France's knee-down tackling after Rassie Erasmus's illegality claim",
          "body": "Springboks head coach Rassie Erasmus branded France's knee-to-ground tackles in last weekend's 21-19 win illegal, but Rugbyrama's review of the match finds most were made with the knee landing at the moment of impact — which keeps them legal. France have drilled the technique for several years under William Servat, their contact-skills coach, to bring tackle height down. Erasmus has been handed a six-week suspension, and Rugbyrama notes it remains to be seen how referees will read the confusion he has sown, ahead of Saturday's test against Argentina."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan moves to No. 8 against South Africa",
          "body": "Wales lose Adam Beard to shoulder injury before Australia test. New Zealand's Damian McKenzie replaces Richie Mo'unga at fly-half. Fiji make hooker Tevita Ikanivere captain for Italy test."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stade de France, Saint-Denis"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Test milestone",
          "heading": "Hugo Keenan to win 50th Ireland cap at full-back against Springboks",
          "body": "Ireland full-back Hugo Keenan brings up his half-century of caps in Saturday's Nations Championship Test against world champions South Africa, Planet Rugby reports. Head coach Andy Farrell names Robert Baloucoune and Mack Hansen on the wings, with Stuart McCloskey and Robbie Henshaw linking up again in midfield and Sam Prendergast partnering Jamison Gibson-Park at half-back. Captain Dan Sheehan, back from concussion, starts at No. 8. The42 reports the Springboks remain 10-point favourites for the game in Dublin."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales lose Adam Beard to shoulder injury before Australia test",
          "body": "New Zealand's Damian McKenzie replaces Richie Mo'unga at fly-half. Fiji make hooker Tevita Ikanivere captain for Italy test."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Aviva Stadium, Dublin",
        "referee": "Christophe Ridley"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility switch",
          "heading": "Domingo Miotti says joking message to Quesada started his road to Italy",
          "body": "Italy fly-half Domingo Miotti, who wins his first cap against Fiji in Udine on Saturday, says his switch began with a congratulatory message to Gonzalo Quesada when his former Jaguares coach became Italy head coach, adding in jest that he had an Italian grandfather. Miotti, whose maternal grandfather was from Lucca, said the idea turned serious over the past year before he raised it with Quesada again this summer. Americas Rugby News reports he turned down a July recall from Argentina head coach Felipe Contepomi to stay eligible."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan moves to No. 8 against South Africa",
