    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-20",
      "edition": "Friday 20 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Jones on Townsend",
          "heading": "Japan coach Eddie Jones says Scotland should be grateful for Gregor Townsend",
          "body": "Japan head coach Eddie Jones used the build-up to Saturday's Nations Championship visit to Murrayfield to back Scotland head coach Gregor Townsend, nine and a half years into the job. \"To do 10 years in charge at a top-eight team in the world is a great accomplishment,\" Jones told BBC Sport, arguing that a country with two professional teams has been knocking on the door of the top four. As England coach, Jones got the better of Townsend only once in five Six Nations meetings."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan moves to No. 8 against South Africa",
