      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Opposition news",
          "heading": "Pumas face Galthié's overhauled France back row with Jalibert recalled at fly-half",
          "body": "France head coach Fabien Galthié has changed his entire back row for Saturday's test against Argentina at the Stade de France. Rugbyrama reports that Charles Ollivon, Anthony Jelonch and Esteban Capilla start, with Grégory Alldritt and Cameron Woki dropping to the bench. Bordeaux-Bègles fly-half Matthieu Jalibert starts at No. 10 in his first outing of any kind since September after injury, Planet Rugby notes, relegating Maxime Lucu to the replacements. France top the northern pool and are chasing next week's final at Twickenham."
        },
