          "heading": "Sir Steve Hansen says Wales loss will help Rennie's All Blacks improve",
          "body": "Former All Blacks head coach Sir Steve Hansen insists New Zealand are improving under current coach Dave Rennie despite last Saturday's 28-35 defeat to Wales — their first in 73 years. Asked on the For The Love Of Rugby podcast whether the side are heading in the right direction, Hansen cited clarity, unity and joy, adding: \"Funnily enough, I think the loss against Wales will actually help them get better.\" He also called the fly-half depth, with Damian McKenzie replacing Richie Mo'unga for Saturday's England test, a luxury worth keeping."
